`rolling_exp_branch_profile_test.py` calls `first_n_items` with five cases: a larger array with smaller `n_desired`, a smaller array with larger `n_desired`, an empty array, a `Variable`, and `n_desired=0` under `pytest.raises`. In `first_n_items`, `if n_desired < 1` is false for the first four calls and true for the last call. `if array.size == 0` is true only for the empty-array call and false otherwise. `if n_desired < array.size` is reached after the empty check; it is true for `np.arange(6), 3` and for the `Variable` of size 3 with `n_desired=2`, and false for `np.arange(2), 5`. After any slicing, `if isinstance(array, Variable)` is true for the `Variable` case and false for the numpy-array cases.

## Answer
{"executed_branches":[{"condition":"n_desired < 1","outcomes":["n_desired < 1 == False","n_desired < 1 == True"]},{"condition":"array.size == 0","outcomes":["array.size == 0 == False","array.size == 0 == True"]},{"condition":"n_desired < array.size","outcomes":["n_desired < array.size == True","n_desired < array.size == False"]},{"condition":"isinstance(array, Variable)","outcomes":["isinstance(array, Variable) == False","isinstance(array, Variable) == True"]}]}
